### B13 tab audio: early, thin, and noisy [light-medium · Robert's ear 2026-09-02 · MEASURE FIRST]
Robert on rec_gpsoujs2sydf (124.8 min, prod, camera + mic + screen + tab audio): "only sound is not perfect, less bass or whatever, tab audio part of second faster than screen video i think, some small noises in tab audio". Three complaints, and only the first has its mechanism named. NO FIX SHIPS BEFORE THE MEASUREMENT — and none of the three is a behaviour Robert has approved changing.
(1) EARLY, and it is measured off the take's own anchors: screen rawAnchor +36.4 ms, system-audio rawAnchor 0 with `reportedInputLatencyMs: 10` SUBTRACTED → effective −10.0 ms. Tab audio is placed 46.4 ms ahead of the picture. Two contributions, both real: video is anchored at frame READ so the picture lands late (X14a's whole subject), and a 10 ms input latency is subtracted from a TAB-AUDIO track — an internal loopback with no microphone and no physical input latency. Chrome reports 10 ms for every device (B7) and measuredAudio subtracts it blind. This is M1 (a)'s twin one channel over, and it may be a one-line fix that needs a measurement first. Note the DIRECTION: this repo's own typical says "40-66 ms, audio LATE"; this take is audio EARLY, and a lead is perceptually ~3× harsher than a lag (~45 ms tolerance vs ~125), which is why he can hear 46 ms.
(2) LESS BASS and (3) SMALL NOISES are one suspect until measured apart: Chrome's voice processing (AEC/NS/AGC) high-passes the bottom, gates quiet passages into artefacts, and downmixes to mono — Robert heard exactly this 2026-08-26 as "mono warble". The take was recorded 177 s after a level-3 wedge, i.e. on the floor rung, which is the rung where the raw flags are most likely to be lost. NOT ESTABLISHED: acquire.ts sends RAW_DISPLAY_AUDIO on EVERY rung including the floor, and `repairDisplayAudio` re-applies the flags to a track that arrives processed. So the suspect is that one of those two belts slipped, not that the design is wrong. Other candidates that must be excluded before blaming the tap: the export mix's makeup gain + u/(1+u) soft limiter (thins bass audibly), opus at 128 kbps stereo, and a stereo→mono collapse anywhere in the chain.
